# 2026-03-26 15:31:23.137987
+Fix the build errors related to missing modules "openai" and "zod" in a robust, production-safe way.
+
+Goals:
+1. Ensure the dependencies "openai" and "zod" are correctly added to package.json under dependencies (not devDependencies).
+2. Ensure the versions are stable and compatible with Next.js 14+ (use widely compatible versions).
+3. Update import usage if necessary to match the installed openai SDK version (modern OpenAI SDK uses `import OpenAI from "openai"` and `openai.responses.create`).
+4. Add defensive handling so the app does not crash if the OpenAI package fails to initialize or if environment variables are missing.
+5. Ensure TypeScript types compile cleanly (no implicit any issues).
+6. Do NOT remove existing functionality—keep the Bourgaeux recommendation logic intact.
+7. Keep the code clean and minimal—no unnecessary abstractions or libraries.
+8. Ensure that after this change, running "npm install && npm run build" succeeds without module resolution errors.
+9. If needed, slightly refactor src/lib/bourgaeux.ts so imports and usage are fully compatible with the installed packages.
+10. Do not break API routes or change their paths.
+
+Important:
+- This is a Next.js App Router project.
+- The goal is to make dependency resolution stable going forward.
+- Avoid introducing any breaking changes to the rest of the app.
+
+After editing, the project should:
+- install cleanly
+- build cleanly
+- still run the recommendation API

